  "hard_gates": [
    "Each old intent needs >=.8 on 10 gate-validation rows AND >=.3 gain from initial validation score; >=6 old intents per source before later-task training.",
    "Later-task learning requires >=6 new intents at >=.8 with >=.3 gain from the acquired-checkpoint phase-start validation score. Old skills require drop >=.3 and final <=.5, all under identical 16-code classification.",
    "All four source receipts required; >=4 forgotten per stream, >=12 TRAIN and >=8 TEST across two disjoint source streams each before any pilot/lens/repair.",
    "Four-intent TRAIN-only repair pilot (two per train stream), no lens, must show >=2 meaningful responses and varied utilities before full lens/action phase.",
    "Full TRAIN-only outcomes then qualify signal and freeze fitted predictors before any heldout action phase.",
    "Retain-only model sees no old training rows and learns the exact same newer-task batches. New intents must reach >=.8 AND gain >=.3 from its own initial validation scores. Its old intents intentionally have no acquisition gate. Heldout reference actions require training repair gates."
